{{- /* The one list of earlyoom arguments, rendered for both init systems:
       etc/default/earlyoom (systemd) and etc/conf.d/earlyoom (OpenRC).
       The two read it differently, so the caller passes the quote that keeps
       each regex one argument: systemd splits $EARLYOOM_ARGS on whitespace
       and keeps quotes, so it gets none; OpenRC evals command_args, so it
       gets single quotes around anything the shell would parse.

       Act at 10% free RAM and swap (SIGTERM) and 5% (SIGKILL), before the
       kernel thrashes on zram. Prefer the processes that piled up in past
       freezes (dozens of parallel shellcheck runs from agent lint hooks,
       hunk viewers), and spare the session, so one big lint dies instead of
       the desktop. Names are /proc/<pid>/comm, at most 15 characters. */ -}}
{{- $q := .quote -}}
-m 10,5 -s 10,5 -r 3600
{{- "" }} --prefer {{ $q }}^(shellcheck|shfmt|hunk)${{ $q }}
{{- "" }} --avoid {{ $q }}^(init|systemd|openrc-init|sshd|dbus-daemon|dbus-broker|dbus-broker-lau|niri|Hyprland|Xwayland|greetd|kitty|zellij|pipewire|wireplumber)${{ $q }}
{{- /* no trailing newline: the callers quote this */ -}}
